# The build context for docker/Dockerfile is the repository root. A clean checkout (what CI builds
# from) is only ~15 MB, so this file is not about CI. It is about a local `make build`: this repo has
# no .gitignore, so an active working directory accumulates untracked target/ (GBs) and benchmarks/
# (tens of GBs) that would otherwise be shipped to the docker daemon on every local build.
#
# .git is deliberately NOT excluded: build.rs runs `git describe --always` and the resulting short
# commit sha becomes part of `trgt --version` (see FULL_VERSION in src/cli.rs). Excluding it would
# silently downgrade the version string to a bare 5.1.0 with no way to tell which commit built it.

target/
benchmarks/
test/
test2/

.memory/
.code_review_local/
.playwright-mcp/
.prompt/
.idea/
.vscode/

*.svg.gz
CLAUDE_HISTORY_*.md
PLAN_*.md
